  "format": "Each case lists its messages in send order. A message is a compact-JSON object (serialized by the runner with separators ',' ':' and ensure_ascii false) or 'raw' text. '@txA' is replaced by txA.raw (generated, see txA below). ids increase from 1 within each case (FD:L2656); each case runs in a fresh session with a full bucket. 'reply' is the expected frame reply: {id, code, data} for errors (message text not normative) or {id, result}. Cases whose B0-B3 outcome can be computed are also executed against tools/bridge_ref.py; routed cases state their downstream criterion. The runner writes every message's exact text, UTF-8 length and sha256 to results/br-messages-expanded.json.",
